Subject: [PATCH] dwc2: use fixed FIFO parameters on the Ingenic X1600 family
Upstream-Status: Pending

Split out of the old
0022-dwc2-remove-3x100ms-overhead-when-booting-with-USB_DR_MODE_OTG-and-Ingenic-X1600.patch.
It carried this change with no explanation whatsoever, under a subject
about removing 100ms delays, alongside unrelated logging and an unrelated
core.c change. It is none of those things and deserves to stand or fall on
its own.

dwc2_get_host_hwparams() and dwc2_get_dev_hwparams() read the FIFO sizes
back out of the hardware, which requires forcing the controller into host
and then device mode during probe. On a usb-role-switch platform each of
those forced transitions costs an IDDIG debounce wait, so the readback
alone adds a large fixed cost to every boot - the reason it was bundled
into a patch about removing delays.

Substitute the known-good values for this SoC family instead of probing for
them. The numbers are the ones the hardware reports on an X1600
(GRXFSIZ/GNPTXFSIZ/HPTXFSIZ after reset) and match the vendor
configuration.

CAVEAT, recorded because the original patch recorded nothing: these values
are asserted for the whole x1600/x1700/x1830/x2000 compatible list but have
only been verified on the X1600 in the Carlinkit Mini Ultra. If another
member of that family ships a different SPRAM size this silently
mis-programs its FIFOs. Anyone enabling one of the other compatibles should
confirm the values first, or narrow the match to "ingenic,x1600-otg".

---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c |  24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
@@ -899,6 +899,14 @@
  * currently in device mode. Should be called immediately after a core
  * soft reset in order to get the reset values.
  */
+static bool dwc2_is_ingenic_x1600_family(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
+{
+	return of_device_is_compatible(hsotg->dev->of_node, "ingenic,x1600-otg") ||
+	       of_device_is_compatible(hsotg->dev->of_node, "ingenic,x1700-otg") ||
+	       of_device_is_compatible(hsotg->dev->of_node, "ingenic,x1830-otg") ||
+	       of_device_is_compatible(hsotg->dev->of_node, "ingenic,x2000-otg");
+}
+
 static void dwc2_get_dev_hwparams(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 {
 	struct dwc2_hw_params *hw = &hsotg->hw_params;
@@ -1007,8 +1015,20 @@
 	 * requires the controller to be in host mode. The mode will
 	 * be forced, if necessary, to read these values.
 	 */
-	dwc2_get_host_hwparams(hsotg);
-	dwc2_get_dev_hwparams(hsotg);
+	if (dwc2_is_ingenic_x1600_family(hsotg)) {
+		int fifo;
+		int fifo_count = dwc2_hsotg_tx_fifo_count(hsotg);
+
+		hw->host_nperio_tx_fifo_size = 3648;
+		hw->host_perio_tx_fifo_size = 1024;
+		hw->dev_nperio_tx_fifo_size = 3648;
+		memset(hw->g_tx_fifo_size, 0, sizeof(hw->g_tx_fifo_size));
+		for (fifo = 1; fifo <= fifo_count; fifo++)
+			hw->g_tx_fifo_size[fifo] = 3648;
+	} else {
+		dwc2_get_host_hwparams(hsotg);
+		dwc2_get_dev_hwparams(hsotg);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
--
